  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    (f : ℝ → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let μ : (n : ℕ) → Measure (Fin n → Bool) := fun n =>\n      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count\n    let S : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ := fun n ε =>\n      (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1\n    let γ : Measure ℝ := gaussianReal 0 1\n    Integrable (fun x => (deriv f x)^2) γ ∧\n    (∀ n : ℕ, Integrable\n      (fun ε : Fin n → Bool => ∑ j : Fin n,\n        (f (S n (Function.update ε j (!ε j))) - f (S n ε))^2) (μ n)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ∫ ε : Fin (n+1) → Bool,\n      (∑ j : Fin (n+1),\n        (f (S (n+1) (Function.update ε j (!ε j))) - f (S (n+1) ε))^2)\n      ∂μ (n+1)) atTop (𝓝 (4 * ∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂γ))",
    "statement_sha256": "9db11af9bdfe47b857fe59ebeea88d5cd2a08f42bb607e42e834b57e88aff462",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "All functions and derivatives are on the real line with the canonical Borel structure. ContDiff Real 2 f means C2; HasCompactSupport f means compact closure of nonzero support. deriv is the real derivative.",
      "For each n, Fin n -> Bool is the actual finite Boolean carrier with canonical finite measurable structure. mu is literal counting measure scaled by inverse actual carrier cardinal in ENNReal. S is the displayed normalized sign sum with true=1 and false=-1; inverse0=0 and Fin0 sum is empty.",
      "gamma=gaussianReal0 1 is the actual mean-zero variance-one real probability Gaussian. Integrable is genuine Bochner integrability, and every displayed integral is a real Bochner integral.",
      "Function.update epsilon j (!epsilon j) replaces only coordinate j by its Boolean negation. The displayed energy is the sum over every coordinate of the squared f-value difference, with no factor one-half.",
      "Only f,C2,compact support are caller inputs. The Gaussian derivative-square domain, every finite-count energy domain including n=0 and the displayed successor full-energy limit are conclusions. No law, domain, bound or convergence certificate is supplied."
    ]
  },
